== ARCHIVE: pytest fastpair stdout, taken after the L2 assertion was made quantitative ==

Archived 2026-10-01. paper/p2.md quotes three numbers that live only in the lines below -
the tau=1e-13 budget reading (cert_err 4.688e-10 Ha against a 1e-9 Ha budget,
-0.523653418 screened against -0.523653446 exact, difference 2.763e-8 kcal/mol) and the
root-separation statement that box_sep equals ball_sep on all 15 atom-block pairs. Their
only carrier until now was nlcsplit/logs/20260929T105823Z_pytest_fastpair_after_assert_fix.out,
which is gitignored scratch, so a reader could not open the thing being cited. The body
below is that file verbatim.

Run: PYTHONPATH=. pytest -q -s on nlcsplit/tests/test_fastpair.py; 10 passed in 432.61 s.
The log line's own timestamp (2026-09-29 10:58 UTC) is the date of the run. The commit
under test is NOT recorded inside the stdout, so this archive does not claim one; what it
does fix is the file content and, below, its hash.
Source SHA-256 (nlcsplit/logs/20260929T105823Z_pytest_fastpair_after_assert_fix.out):
cf2540dc382dc256d7d6af02e19338beec130b561deafebd15c07a710facefb8

Two cautions for anyone reading the sweep as a cost curve:
  * "省下的点对占比" is the droppable fraction of far+self point pairs, so the evaluated
    fraction is its complement (9.81% dropped = 90.19% evaluated at tau=1e-13);
  * these are functional measurements printed from inside tests, not the timed runs in
    evidence/scaling/, which are the only admissible cost numbers.

